      ],
      "form_arabic": "طَرِيقًا",
      "lemma": "Tariyq",
      "lemma_arabic": "طَرِيق",
      "pos": "N",
      "ayah_id": "4:168",
      "ayah_arabic": "إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ وَظَلَمُواْ لَمۡ يَكُنِ ٱللَّهُ لِيَغۡفِرَ لَهُمۡ وَلَا لِيَهۡدِيَهُمۡ طَرِيقًا",
      "surah_revelation": "Medinan",
      "surah_name": "An-Nisaa",
      "literal_gloss": "(to) a way",
      "translations": {
        "saheeh": "Indeed, those who disbelieve and commit wrong [or injustice] - never will Allah forgive them, nor will He guide them to a path.",
        "pickthall": "Lo! those who disbelieve and deal in wrong, Allah will never forgive them, neither will He guide them unto a road,",
        "khattab": "Those who disbelieve and wrong themselves—surely Allah will neither forgive them nor guide them to any path",
        "arberry": "Surely the unbelievers, who have done evil, God would not forgive them, neither guide them on any road"
      }
    },
    {
      "location": [
        4,
        169,
        2
      ],
      "form_arabic": "طَرِيقَ",
      "lemma": "Tariyq",
      "lemma_arabic": "طَرِيق",
      "pos": "N",
      "ayah_id": "4:169",
      "ayah_arabic": "إِلَّا طَرِيقَ جَهَنَّمَ خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَآ أَبَدࣰ اۚ وَكَانَ ذَٰلِكَ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ يَسِيرࣰ ا",
      "surah_revelation": "Medinan",
      "surah_name": "An-Nisaa",
      "literal_gloss": "(the) way",
      "translations": {
        "saheeh": "Except the path of Hell; they will abide therein forever. And that, for Allah, is [always] easy.",
        "pickthall": "Except the road of hell, wherein they will abide for ever. And that is ever easy for Allah.",
        "khattab": "except that of Hell, to stay there for ever and ever. And that is easy for Allah",
        "arberry": "but the road to Gehenna, therein dwelling forever and ever; and that for God is an easy matter."
      }
    },
    {
      "location": [
        20,
        63,
        12
      ],
      "form_arabic": "بِطَرِيقَتِكُمُ",
      "lemma": "Tariyqap",
      "lemma_arabic": "طَرِيقَة",
      "pos": "N",
      "ayah_id": "20:63",
      "ayah_arabic": "قَالُوٓاْ إِنۡ هَٰذَٰنِ لَسَٰحِرَٰنِ يُرِيدَانِ أَن يُخۡرِجَاكُم مِّنۡ أَرۡضِكُم بِسِحۡرِهِمَا وَيَذۡهَبَا بِطَرِيقَتِكُمُ ٱلۡمُثۡلَىٰ",
      "surah_revelation": "Meccan",
      "surah_name": "Taa-Haa",
      "literal_gloss": "with your way",
      "translations": {
        "saheeh": "They said, \"Indeed, these are two magicians who want to drive you out of your land with their magic and do away with your most exemplary way.",
        "pickthall": "They said: Lo! these are two wizards who would drive you out from your country by their magic, and destroy your best traditions;",
        "khattab": "They concluded, “These two are only magicians who want to drive you out of your land with their magic, and do away with your most cherished traditions",
        "arberry": "saying, 'These two men are sorcerers and their purpose is to expel you out of your land by their sorcery, and to extirpate your justest way."
      }
    },
    {
      "location": [
        20,
        77,
        10
      ],
      "form_arabic": "طَرِيقًا",
      "lemma": "Tariyq",
      "lemma_arabic": "طَرِيق",
      "pos": "N",
      "ayah_id": "20:77",
      "ayah_arabic": "وَلَقَدۡ أَوۡحَيۡنَآ إِلَىٰ مُوسَىٰٓ أَنۡ أَسۡرِ بِعِبَادِي فَٱضۡرِبۡ لَهُمۡ طَرِيقࣰ ا فِي ٱلۡبَحۡرِ يَبَسࣰ ا لَّا تَخَٰفُ دَرَكࣰ ا وَلَا تَخۡشَىٰ",
      "surah_revelation": "Meccan",
      "surah_name": "Taa-Haa",
      "literal_gloss": "a path",
      "translations": {
        "saheeh": "And We had inspired to Moses, \"Travel by night with My servants and strike for them a dry path through the sea; you will not fear being overtaken [by Pharaoh] nor be afraid [of drowning].\"",
        "pickthall": "And verily We inspired Moses, saying: Take away My slaves by night and strike for them a dry path in the sea, fearing not to be overtaken, neither being afraid (of the sea).",
        "khattab": "And We surely inspired Moses, ˹saying,˺ “Leave with My servants ˹at night˺ and strike a dry passage for them across the sea. Have no fear of being overtaken, nor be concerned ˹of drowning˺.”",
        "arberry": "Also We revealed unto Moses, 'Go with My servants by night; strike for them a dry path in the sea, fearing not overtaking, neither afraid.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "location": [
        20,
        104,
        8
      ],
      "form_arabic": "طَرِيقَةً",
      "lemma": "Tariyqap",
      "lemma_arabic": "طَرِيقَة",
      "pos": "N",
      "ayah_id": "20:104",
      "ayah_arabic": "نَّحۡنُ أَعۡلَمُ بِمَا يَقُولُونَ إِذۡ يَقُولُ أَمۡثَلُهُمۡ طَرِيقَةً إِن لَّبِثۡتُمۡ إِلَّا يَوۡمࣰ ا",
      "surah_revelation": "Meccan",
      "surah_name": "Taa-Haa",
      "literal_gloss": "(in) conduct",
      "translations": {
        "saheeh": "We are most knowing of what they say when the best of them in manner will say, \"You remained not but one day.\"",
        "pickthall": "We are Best Aware of what they utter when their best in conduct say: Ye have tarried but a day.",
        "khattab": "We know best what they will say—the most reasonable of them will say, “You stayed no more than a day.”",
        "arberry": "We know very well what they will say, when the justest of them in the way will say, 'You have tarried only a day.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "location": [
        23,
        17,
        5
      ],
      "form_arabic": "طَرَا^ئِقَ",
      "lemma": "Tariyqap",
      "lemma_arabic": "طَرِيقَة",
      "pos": "N",
      "ayah_id": "23:17",
      "ayah_arabic": "وَلَقَدۡ خَلَقۡنَا فَوۡقَكُمۡ سَبۡعَ طَرَآئِقَ وَمَا كُنَّا عَنِ ٱلۡخَلۡقِ غَٰفِلِينَ",
